window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-057", "name_zh": "片刻点", "name_en": "moment point", "tagline": "赛斯把每个「现在」讲成一片行动的范围，而不是时间线上的一个点——自我只看得见它的一角，你其他的部分却能从它走进去。", "explanation": "片刻点是赛斯在早期课第 149 至 152 节（1965 年）提出的单位：它不是一小段时间，而是你在当下能吸收、能纳入的一整套行动，是从广阔的现在里任意切出的一个切点。自我正好立在切点上，被它聚焦也被它囚住，于是把实相经验成一串前后相接的时刻；潜意识与内我的其他部分不受此限，能同时包覆许多片刻点，并把它们当作从一个活动场域通往另一个的入口或通道。由此得出几个结论：人的一生不过是一个片刻点；你更大的意识同时在好几个片刻点上生成肉身，那些一生并非前后相接；梦、创造与艺术都是穿行于片刻点的旅行。拉到最大尺度，整个物质宇宙也只是总体设计当中的一个片刻点。", "definitions": [{"zh": "基本上，片刻点并不是由任何特定的时段构成的，而是在你们系统之内的一个方便用语，表达或代表不用过度费力就可以方便纳入的实相范围。", "en": "A moment point basically consists not of any particular given time division, but is within your system a convenient term that expresses or represents the range of reality that can be conveniently embraced without undue strain.", "source": "Session 150"}, {"zh": "在你们所谓的一个片刻之内，很多这样的感知闪现而过，影响了任何既定的个体。不过，在你们的系统之内，有机体能够有效组织这些感知之前，有一个时间间隔。我所说的片刻点只是你们物理时刻的一个近似值而已。这里我正在设法解释清楚的是，行动范围才是重点。片刻点就是一套行动。", "en": "Within what you call one moment, many such perceptions flash through to affect any given individual. However there is within your system a lapse before the organism can effectively organize these perceptions. My idea of a moment point is only an approximation of your physical moment. I am trying to make it plain here that the range of action is what is important. A moment point is a range of action.", "source": "Session 150"}, {"zh": "片刻点本身就是任意界定的，是一种人工的区分。我们说过，对你们来说，片刻点其实是由你们在当下的架构之内能够吸收的行动数量所组成，因为片刻点实际上是广阔现在的一部分。", "en": "The moment point is in itself arbitrary, an artificial division. As we have said, the moment point for you is actually composed of the amount of action which you are capable of assimilating within your present framework, for the moment point is indeed a portion of the spacious present.", "source": "Session 151"}, {"zh": "我告诉你们我们不感受你们的时间顺序，我们只游历过不同的强度。我们的工作、发展与经验，全发生在我所谓的“瞬点”内。此地，在瞬点内，最微细的思想已有了结果，最微不足道的可能性已被探索，彻底地检查过所有的可能性，最弱或最强的感受都照应到了。这很难解释清楚，但瞬点即我们的心理经验在其内发生的那个架构。在其中，同时的行动按照联想的模式彼此“自由”地相随。举例来说，假装我想到了你，约瑟。而当我如此做时，我立刻便完全感受到你的过去、现在与未来（对你而言），以及所有曾主宰过你的强烈或决定性的情感与动机。如果我高兴的话，我可能与你一起同游过那些经验。例如，用你们的话来说，在一眨眼的功夫，我们能跟随一个意识，经历它所有的形式。", "en": "I told you that we do not experience your time sequence. We travel through various intensities. Our work, development, and experience all takes place within what I term the “moment point.” Here, within the moment point, the smallest thought is brought to fruition, the slightest possibility explored, the probabilities thoroughly examined, the least or the most forceful feeling entertained. It is difficult to explain this clearly, and yet the moment point is the framework within which we have our psychological experience. Within it, simultaneous actions follow “freely” through associative patterns. For example, pretend that I think of you, Joseph. In so doing I immediately experience — and fully — your past, present, and future (in your terms), and all of those strong or determining emotions and motivations that have ruled you. I can travel through those experiences with you, if I choose. We can follow a consciousness through all of its forms, for example, and in your terms, within the flicker of an eye.", "source": "Session 514"}, {"zh": "以你们的话来说——这句话是必要的——片刻点（the moment point）（注四）、当下这一刻，是所有的存在与实相之间的交会点，所有的可能性流过它，虽然你们的一个片刻点可以被体验为你为其一部分的其他可能实相里的几世纪或一次呼吸。", "en": "In your terms — the phrase is necessary — the moment point,5 the present, is the point of interaction between all existences and reality. All probabilities flow through it, though one of your moment points may be experienced as centuries, or as a breath, in other probable realities of which you are a part.", "source": "Session 681"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "它是什么：一片行动的范围，不是一小段时间", "note": "赛斯先把最容易误会的地方堵死：片刻点不是一段被切出来的时间。第 150 节说它「并不是由任何特定的时段构成的」，只是你们系统里的一个方便用语，代表你不费力气就能纳入的那一段实相；同一节随即给了正面说法——**片刻点就是一套行动**，它只是你物理时刻的一个近似值。第 151 节再补一句「它本身就是任意界定的，是一种人工的区分」，因为它实际是广阔现在的一部分，大小取决于你在当下的架构里能吸收多少行动。第 152 节拆掉最后一层：这样的点有它自己的分子结构，那是行动强化出来的结果，跟它正好落在你钟表上的哪一刻「基本上毫无关联」。尺度于是也变了：第 219 节叫它「任何一个当下的一瞬间」，并让你从唐尼（Dunne）那套「自我一在时间一里看到的这个点」起步；《未知的实相》第 681 节把定义压成一句——片刻点、当下这一刻，是所有存在与实相之间的交会点，所有的可能性都从它流过；第 343 节说得最直白，片刻点确实由行动组成，而那些行动本身就在自我体验。", "src": "早期课第5册第 219 节；早期课第4册第 150、151、152 节；早期课第8册第 343 节；未知的实相卷一第 681 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 150 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 152 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 343 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 681 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0027", "zh": "现在如果你们记得我们前几节课讨论过的价值完成，让我们现在来想想所谓的片刻点。这个片刻点，如你所知的，指的是现在的一瞬间。如果你以唐尼的理论来想，片刻点可以看作是自己一的时间一。", "en": "Now. If you will recall our early sessions dealing with value fulfillment, let us now consider what I prefer to call a moment point. This moment point, as you know, refers to any given present instant. If you are thinking in terms of Dunnes theories, then start out with this moment point as it is seen in time one by self one.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0004", "zh": "现在。我们要努力继续来谈一些上一节讨论的事情。基本上，片刻点并不是由任何特定的时段构成的，而是在你们系统之内的一个方便用语，表达或代表不用过度费力就可以方便纳入的实相范围。", "en": "Now. We will endeavor to continue speaking of some matters discussed in our previous session. A moment point basically consists not of any particular given time division, but is within your system a convenient term that expresses or represents the range of reality that can be conveniently embraced without undue strain.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第150节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "150", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0005", "zh": "在你们所谓的一个片刻之内，很多这样的感知闪现而过，影响了任何既定的个体。不过，在你们的系统之内，有机体能够有效组织这些感知之前，有一个时间间隔。我所说的片刻点只是你们物理时刻的一个近似值而已。这里我正在设法解释清楚的是，行动范围才是重点。片刻点就是一套行动。", "en": "Within what you call one moment, many such perceptions flash through to affect any given individual. However there is within your system a lapse before the organism can effectively organize these perceptions. My idea of a moment point is only an approximation of your physical moment. I am trying to make it plain here that the range of action is what is important. A moment point is a range of action.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第150节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "150", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0007", "zh": "原则上我们这里主要是在探讨行动的本质，而且实质上所有表面的区分都是为了解释而任意为之。片刻点本身就是任意界定的，是一种人工的区分。我们说过，对你们来说，片刻点其实是由你们在当下的架构之内能够吸收的行动数量所组成，因为片刻点实际上是广阔现在的一部分。", "en": "We are dealing here principally, and in the main, with the essence of action, and essentially all apparent divisions are arbitrary for the sake of explanation. The moment point is in itself arbitrary, an artificial division. As we have said, the moment point for you is actually composed of the amount of action which you are capable of assimilating within your present framework, for the moment point is indeed a portion of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0022", "zh": "附带一提，这些片刻点具有通道或入口的作用，通常从某一个活动场域到另一个。这样一个片刻点有其特殊的分子结构，那是行动强化的结果，虽然这个片刻点会碰巧符合你们物理时间所谓的时刻，但基本上两者毫无关联。", "en": "These moment points, incidentally, serve as reference points often from one field of activity to another, as openings or entryways. Such a moment point has a peculiar molecular structure, that is a result of intensification of action, and basically has nothing to do with the moment point happening to coincide with what you call a physical moment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第152节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "152", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0052", "zh": "片刻点实际上是由行动组成，而这些行动本身就会自我体验。你们在物质层面上所看到和体验到的，代表一小部分而已，充其量只是所谓实相的一丁点，宇宙之中还有宇宙。行动就是经验，而且会形成自己的经验。思想是一种电磁模式，会将自己具体化为宇宙系统。你的肉体是一系列的行动，而使用系列一词只是为了方便起见。", "en": "Now. Moment points are indeed composed of action, action experiencing itself. What you see and experience physically represents but a small portion, a mere fraction of what reality is. There are universes within universes. Action is, and yet forms its own experience. Thoughts take electromagnetic patterns that have their own materializations as universal systems. Your physical body is a series of actions, though the word series is being used for simplicity's sake only.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0080", "zh": "以你们的话来说——这句话是必要的——片刻点（the moment point）、当下这一刻，是所有的存在与实相之间的交会点，所有的可能性流过它，虽然你们的一个片刻点可以被体验为你为其一部分的其他可能实相里的几世纪或一次呼吸。", "en": "In your terms — the phrase is necessary — the moment point,5 the present, is the point of interaction between all existences and reality. All probabilities flow through it, though one of your moment points may be experienced as centuries, or as a breath, in other probable realities of which you are a part.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第681节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "681", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0054", "zh": "我就努力把这一点讲清楚，片刻点具有电磁结构。", "en": "Now. I am trying to make this clear. Moment points have a structure, electro magnetically.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它不是一个「点」：行动从切点朝四面八方展开", "note": "第 149 节给了这一页最重要的画面。你把自己经验成沿一条线移动，线上每个点代表时间中的一个片刻；但**在代表任何片刻的那个点上，行动朝四面八方往外移动**——从那个片刻点的立场看，行动形成一个想像的圆，而它就是圆顶的切点，且这发生在每一个片刻点上。所以第 151 节说，每一个片刻点都是一个场域或一个维度：你只感知它极受限的几个面向，同一个片刻点被另一套感知者经验时，面貌与你们所见大异其趣。第 219 节接着说，自我看不见这个点是**敞开**的——它代表通往许多其他维度的开口，那些维度可以被走过，只是自我那套肉体装备走不了；同一节把它的性质说成强度：片刻点全是强度、是电性实相，穿过这类维度就是能量从一个强度转变成另一个强度，而把这些自己分隔开来只是为了讨论，一流行分隔就几乎改掉了我们要研究的那东西的本质。第 343 节给出一体两面的说法：片刻点一方面是行动的一个极细微的部分，另一方面是通往未知可能性与新维度的入口——你一探进去，就自动成为它的一部分并把它改掉。", "src": "第 149、151、219、343 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 343 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0003", "zh": "因此，就一连串的物理片刻而言，为了价值完成，某一部分物质成长必须在物质有机体之内显现才行。在梦领域以及很多其他系统之内，这一连串的片刻是未知的。发展并不是来自沿着单一方向，一个接一个直线式产生的一连串行动。相反地，发展主要就是价值完成这码事，透过行动的视角而达成，透过在任何行动之内的旅行、顺随它，跟着它改变而达成。讲得更清楚一点好了，我说过行动存在于无限的视角之内，你们所熟悉的多半是在物质系统内，沿着单一连续路线的物质化行动。然后你们体验行动，好像你们正沿着单一线条移动似的，这条线上的每个点代表你们时间中的一个片刻。但是在你们的线条上，代表着任何片刻的一个想像的点上，行动朝着四面八方往外移动。从那个片刻点的立场看来，你们可以想像行动形成一个想像的圆，而那个片刻点就是切点（apex）。但是，这发生在每一个片刻点上。", "en": "A certain portion of physical growth, in terms of a series of physical moments, is therefore necessary for value fulfillment to show itself within a physical organism. Within the dream field and within many other systems, this series of moments is unknown. Development comes not from a series of actions strung out along a single line, one before the other in lengthwise fashion. Instead development is largely a matter of value fulfillment, which is achieved through the perspectives of action, through traveling within any given action, and following it and changing with it. To make this clearer, I have said that action exists within limitless perspectives, and that you are mainly familiar with it as it is materialized along a single line of continuity within the physical system. You experience action then as if you were moving along a single line, each dot on the line representing a moment of your time. But at the imaginary point on your line that represents any given moment, action moves out in all directions. From the standpoint of that moment point, you could imagine action forming an imaginary circle with that point as an apex. But this happens at the point of every moment.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0016", "zh": "现在。每一个片刻点都是一个场域或维度。你们只感知若干这类片刻点某些相当受限的面向而已。同样的片刻点可能同时以完全不同的方式体验，然后产生一套不同的感知。这些片刻点呈现出来的面貌，与你们所见大异其趣。", "en": "Now. Each moment point is a field or dimension. You perceive certain very limited aspects of a given number of such moment points. The same moment points may simultaneously be experienced in an entirely different fashion, and to a different set of perceptions. These moment points would appear quite different than they appear to you.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0030", "zh": "自我无法看见这个片刻点是开放的，可以说它代表了很多其他维度的开口。这些维度可以被旅行过；但它们不是被自我旅行过，因为自我只能察觉到那些物质装备可以看见或注意到的维度。", "en": "The ego cannot see that this moment point is open, so to speak, and represents an opening into many other dimensions. These dimensions may be traveled through; but they may not be traveled through by the ego, for the ego can only perceive those dimensions which it is physically equipped to see, or perceive.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0033", "zh": "唐尼到这个阶段是对的。但重点是，如果你允许我一语双关，这些片刻点是所有的强度，电性实相，而旅行过这类维度涉及了能量从一个强度转变成另一个强度。全我，或我所说的存有，是由所有这些自己们组成，但基本上来说，必须了解的是，这些自己们的所有分隔都是幻相。为了讨论，我们区隔它们，但这么做之后，我们几乎改变了我们试图研究的、它们的基本本质。", "en": "To this degree Dunne was correct. But the important point, if you will forgive a pun, is that these moment points are all intensities, electrical realities, and traveling through such dimensions involves a transformation of energy from one intensity to another. The whole self, or the entity of which I speak, is composed of all of these selves, but it must be realized that all divisions between these selves are illusions, basically speaking. For the sake of discussion we separate them, but in doing so we almost manage to change the very nature of that which we attempt to study.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0056", "zh": "内在感官可以让你跟随其中的一些行动进入其他实相中。片刻点一方面当然是属于行动的一个细微部分，另一方面，也是一个进入未知的可能性和新维度的入口。当你探索任何一个片刻点，随着它对你产生了印象，你自动会成为它的一部分，也改变它。这些交互影响发生在许多层面上：心理、化学、电磁及心灵上。如你所知，你影响且形成自己的物质环境，它也反过来形成你，此时，你所知的自己便在刹那间产生了细微变化，这只是在物质层面上发生的事。", "en": "The inner senses allow you to follow some of these actions into other realities. The moment point on the one hand is of course a minute division of action. On the other hand it is an entrance into unknown possibilities and new dimensions. As you probe into any given moment point, you automatically become a part of it and change it accordingly as it makes its impressions upon you. These interchanging’s occur on many levels: psychologically, chemically, electromagnetically, psychically. There are subtle variations, as you know, in your known self from one instant to another as you affect your physical environment and form it, and as it in turn forms you. And this is just on the physical level.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "自我站在切点上：被它聚焦，也被它囚住", "note": "这一块回答一个日常感觉：为什么时间对「我」过得这么慢、这么一小口一小口。第 151 节：就自我与行动、与片刻点的关系而言，**自我就是自己立于片刻点切点之上的那一部分**，被完全聚焦在它上面、也被它囚禁在那一部分自己里；只有自我从这一刻迈向下一刻，像一个人从一个水坑走到另一个水坑，也只有它会淹没在时间当中。它之所以焦点如此精准鲜明，恰恰因为范围小——在有限的疆域里，刺激与回应都有强度。第 219 节给了同一意思的视觉版：自我看片刻点，像看一串从一侧靠近、从另一侧穿过的光，一个平的、硬纸板般的物件在面前闪过就消失，它只能意识到任何当下瞬间的一部分。反面是其他那些自己：第 151 节说潜意识以及除了自我以外自己的每一部分，都能吸收范围更大的行动，向内也向外延伸，因而包覆许多个片刻点——对你而言的一个片刻，对它们几乎是无可限量的片刻，因为没有经验、没有行动，连物理时间都毫无意义。第 152 节把这条线落到实用上：连个人潜意识都远比自我不受片刻点束缚，它知道哪些发展可能大有帮助，会回过头通知自我。", "src": "第 151、152、219 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 152 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0009", "zh": "潜意识以及自己的每一部分，事实上除了自我以外，都有能力吸收范围更大的行动。因此，时间本质对这些其他部分的自己来说，和自我的时间本质大为不同。自我的确有很多面向，可以从它和很多其他实相面向的关系来定义它。就它和行动，以及片刻点的关系而言，自我的确是自己立于片刻点的切点之上的那一部分，受到片刻点的限制。在这个背景中，自我就是被完全聚焦在片刻点之上，也被它囚禁在那一部分自己。", "en": "The subconscious, and in fact all portions of the self with the exception of the ego, are capable of assimilating a wider area, so to speak, of action. Therefore to these other portions of the self, time has a much different essence than it has for the ego. The ego is indeed many things. It can be defined in relationship to many other aspects of reality. In relationship to action, and moment points, the ego is indeed that portion of the self which stands at the apex of the moment point, and is limited by the moment point. The ego is in this context the portion of the self which is utterly focused upon, and imprisoned by, the moment point.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0029", "zh": "自我只能意识到特定的片刻点，或当下一瞬间的一部分，它看着片刻点就像它是一连串从一个方向靠近自我的光之一，且从另一个方向通过它。自我感知到这个片刻点，接着就好像它像个平的、厚纸板般的物件而来，在它面前闪过，然后消失。", "en": "The ego can perceive only certain portions of any given moment point or present instant, and it sees the moment point indeed as if it were one of a series of lights that approaches the ego from one side, and passes him by on the other side. The ego perceives this moment point, then, very much as if it were a flat cardboard-like object which comes, is flashed before him, and disappears.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0010", "zh": "不过，潜意识没有这样的限制。如果你们考虑到位于片刻点切点上的自我，以及它因此被囚禁在它自己的先后（begore-and-after）、因果(cause-and-effect)经验界域之内，就能够想像潜意识进一步往外延伸，抓住很多其他片刻点。如此一来，自我的焦点为何如此精准和鲜明，原因应该显而易见了。在它有限的范围之内，刺激和回应有其强度。没错，自我就是专门贯注在某个既定行动场域或维度的那一部分人格。", "en": "The subconscious however is not so limited. If you consider the ego at the apex of the moment point, and imprisoned therefore within the realm of its own before-and-after, cause-and-effect experience, then you can imagine the subconscious reaching further outward and seizing upon many other moment points. It should be easy to see then why the focus of the ego is so sharp and brilliant. Within its limited scope there is intensity of stimuli and response. Indeed, the ego is that portion of the personality which is plunged into a specific and intense preoccupation with a given field of action or dimension.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0011", "zh": "潜意识既向外延伸也向内延伸，在广阔的现在之内没有真正的过去、现在和未来，所以的确有无限的内在和外在；而且再一次，行动之内的行动也是无限的，这些行动永无止境，因为它们是自生的。所以，内我的其他部分甚至向四面八方延伸得更远，因此包覆很多片刻点。于是，对内我的很多部分而言，你们所谓的一个片刻，就相当于一个几乎无可限量的片刻，因为没有了经验，没有了行动，连物理时间都毫无意义。", "en": "The subconscious, reaching outward, reaches also inward. For while there is no real past or present or future within the spacious present, there is indeed an infinity of inward and outward; and again, of actions within actions, and there is no end to these actions for they are self-generating. The other portions of the inner self reach then even further in all directions, and they therefore envelop many moment points. To many portions of the inner self then, what you would call a moment would correspond to an almost limitless number of moments, for even physical time has no meaning without experience without action.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0012", "zh": "只有自我是从这一刻迈向下一刻，就像一个人从一个水坑走到另一个水坑一样。也只有自我会淹没在时间当中。由于只有自我被短暂囚禁在你们层面的焦点中，所以只有它这么慢吞吞地探索同时的行动，一小块一小块、一小口一小口地感知它。所以你们现在就知道我说无限的自己是什么意思。因为全我并没有这样被束缚住，全我能够也确实同时感知无数这样的片刻点。现在仔细听：", "en": "It is only the ego that steps from moment to moment, as a man who walks from puddle to puddle. It is only the ego who drowns in time. Therefore, since only the ego is momentarily imprisoned within the focus of your plane, it is only the ego who probes so slowly into simultaneous action, perceiving it bit by bit and sip by sip. So now you will see what I meant when I spoke about the limitless self, for the whole self is not so bound. The whole self could and does perceive a limitless number of such moment points simultaneously. And now hear this:", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0020", "zh": "在任何当下人格的成形过程中，个人潜意识和自我的确是对等的伙伴，鲁柏的成果是他训练有成的证据。一旦自我和潜意识之间建立这样的关系，那么这两者之间的沟通一般而言都会持续改善。潜意识，甚至是个人潜意识，远比自我更不受片刻点的束缚，而且它还会通知自我，可能会大有帮助的重要发展是什么。", "en": "The personal subconscious and the ego are indeed equal partners in the formation of any given present personality. Ruburt’s results are evidence that his training is bearing fruit. Once such a relationship is set up between the ego and the subconscious, then communication in general between the two will always improve. The subconscious, even the personal subconscious, is much freer from the moment point than is the ego, and it can inform the ego of important developments which can be of great help.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第152节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "152", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "它是从「广阔的现在」里切出来的", "note": "这一页最需要防的误读，是把片刻点当成时间的最小颗粒。第 151 节一开始就把三样东西绑在一起讲：我们谈过的片刻点、广阔的现在，以及全我里你称之为潜意识的那一部分，「的确有关联」。第 241 节讲得更硬：**在把广阔的现在这个观念讲清楚之前，赛斯根本没法向你解释片刻点**——先有那个过去、现在、未来同时存在的现在，才谈得上从里面取出的切点；第 151 节因此说，片刻点实际上就是广阔现在的一部分。另一头连着价值完成：第 151 节预告「还会有更多与片刻点和价值完成相关的资料」，因为价值完成是一切系统、一切经验背后的理由，它看似依赖你们所知的时间，那只反映你感知时间的方式，一点也没改变它同时性的本质。第 269 节把尺度一次给足：人的一生寿命不过是一个片刻点，而自我正是你用来深入探索这个片刻点的那部分；价值完成需要感知的这种减速——你甚至能在几个物理时刻之内得到完全独立于你们时间结构的经验，这就是心理时间的用法。第 305 节最后接上无限：无限与你所知的空间或时间一点关系都没有，它是「变为」的状态，与价值完成、全新可能性的开展、片刻点的探索、以及穿越不断创造时间幻相的维度之旅有关。", "src": "第 151、241、269、305 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 241 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 269 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 305 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0006", "zh": "对于我们才开始触及的很多主题，要解释的还很多，因为所有东西都相互关联；我们谈过的片刻点、广阔的现在，以及全我当中你们称之为潜意识的那一部分之间，的确有关联。", "en": "There is much to be explained along many lines which we have only begun to touch upon, for all things are correlated; and there is indeed a correlation between our moment points of which we have spoken, the spacious present, and that portion of the whole self which you call the subconscious.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0037", "zh": "例如，直到我清楚说明广阔的现在这个观念之前，我无法向你解释片刻点。这并不像它表面看起来那么简单，因为其中不涉及任何强制，所以鲁柏向来都是同意让我把概念塞给他，而他在我的协助下以说话的方式解读。", "en": "I could not have explained moment points to you, for example, until I had clearly given the idea of the spacious present. It is not as simple a thing as it might seem, for there is no coercion involved, Ruburt always consenting to let me push concepts at him, which he interprets speech-wise with my assistance.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第241节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "241", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0019", "zh": "这里也会有更多与片刻点和价值完成相关的资料，因为价值完成是所有系统，以及你们场域之内所有经验背后的理由。我提过，价值完成似乎，而且或多或少取决于你们所知的时间，但这只反映在你们感知时间的方式，绝对没有改变价值完成的同时性本质，它在维度里成长，但不是取决于你们所知的时间。", "en": "There will be much more here also concerning moment points and value fulfillment. For this, value fulfillment, is the reason behind the existence of all systems, and of all experience within your field. I mentioned that value fulfillment seems, and is to some small degree, dependent upon time as you know it, but this merely reflects upon the manner in which you perceive time, and in no way alters the simultaneous nature of value fulfillment, which grows in dimension but is not dependent upon time as you know it.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0046", "zh": "人的一生寿命不过是一个片刻点而已。自我是你能够用来探索和体验这个片刻点的那个部分。(微笑）价值完成需要感知的这种减速。这很难解释。想想心理时间的运用。你在物理时间的几个物理时刻之内获得经验，这些经验完全独立于你们的时间结构之外。", "en": "The span of a whole man’s lifetime is no more than a moment point. The ego is the portion of you equipped to explore and experience this moment point in depth. （Smile.） Value fulfillment demands this slowing down of perception. This is most difficult to explain. Consider using psychological time. You have experiences within a few physical moments of physical time, experiences that are entirely independent of your time structure.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第269节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "269", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0050", "zh": "无限与你所知的空间或时间一点关系都没有。无限是变为的状态，而且永远不可能结束，因为它永远不会完成。无限与价值完成，以及全新可能性的开展、片刻点的探索、穿越不断创造时间幻相的维度之旅有关系。但是，既然没有时间，有什么好结束的呢？", "en": "Infinity has nothing to do with space or time as you know it. Infinity is the state of becoming and can never have an end for it is never completed. Infinity has to do with value fulfillment, and the unfoldings of ever new possibilities, the exploration of moment points, the traveling through dimensions that ever creates the illusion of time. But since there is no time, what is there to end?", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第305节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "305", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "时间不是一条片刻点的链：连续感从哪来", "note": "第 41 节（1963 年，这批资料最早的一处）就把「一个片刻接一个片刻」当成一种可选的理论：没有一个连续的片刻点也可以有秩序，没有你们的因果关系也可以有秩序——秩序可以在自发性里、在广阔的现在的同时性存在里，而且的确已经有了。同一节话说得很清醒：连续时间的理念在你们这个层面上目前还行得通，等人类更有野心时它在理论上就会被舍弃，但你还是会继续造桌子、继续戴表。第 248 节点出界线立在哪里：你只感知任何既定行动的一小部分，当你不再感知它，对你来说行动本身就停止了，于是人为的界限于焉树立。第 357 节把结论说明白：时间根本不是以一系列片刻点的方式存在，这是三维度的幻觉，因此实际上没有哪一世活在另一世之前或之后。第 430 节拿另一种经验方式作对照：从未在你们物质系统里存在过的人格，不以任何时间顺序经验事件——片刻点被**全然**经验，种种开展同时打开，「事件」被认作心灵与心理的发生，不一定与任何外在环境相连。《灵魂永生》第 514 节是这一块的枢纽（中译作「瞬点」，英文就是 moment point）：我们不感受你们的时间顺序，只游历不同的强度；我们的工作、发展与经验全发生在片刻点之内——它是心理经验于其中发生的那个架构，最微细的思想在里面有了结果、最微不足道的可能性被探索，同时的行动按照联想的模式彼此自由相随。", "src": "灵魂永生第 514 节；早期课第1册第 41 节；早期课第6册第 248 节；早期课第8册第 343、357 节；早期课第9册第 430 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 514 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 248 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 343 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 357 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 430 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0074", "zh": "我告诉你们我们不感受你们的时间顺序，我们只游历过不同的强度。我们的工作、发展与经验，全发生在我所谓的“瞬点”内。此地，在瞬点内，最微细的思想已有了结果，最微不足道的可能性已被探索，彻底地检查过所有的可能性，最弱或最强的感受都照应到了。这很难解释清楚，但瞬点即我们的心理经验在其内发生的那个架构。在其中，同时的行动按照联想的模式彼此“自由”地相随。举例来说，假装我想到了你，约瑟。而当我如此做时，我立刻便完全感受到你的过去、现在与未来（对你而言），以及所有曾主宰过你的强烈或决定性的情感与动机。如果我高兴的话，我可能与你一起同游过那些经验。例如，用你们的话来说，在一眨眼的功夫，我们能跟随一个意识，经历它所有的形式。", "en": "I told you that we do not experience your time sequence. We travel through various intensities. Our work, development, and experience all takes place within what I term the “moment point.” Here, within the moment point, the smallest thought is brought to fruition, the slightest possibility explored, the probabilities thoroughly examined, the least or the most forceful feeling entertained. It is difficult to explain this clearly, and yet the moment point is the framework within which we have our psychological experience. Within it, simultaneous actions follow “freely” through associative patterns. For example, pretend that I think of you, Joseph. In so doing I immediately experience — and fully — your past, present, and future (in your terms), and all of those strong or determining emotions and motivations that have ruled you. I can travel through those experiences with you, if I choose. We can follow a consciousness through all of its forms, for example, and in your terms, within the flicker of an eye.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第514节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "514", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0001", "zh": "没有一个连续的片刻点，也可以有秩序。没有你们的因果关系，信不信由你，也一样可以有秩序。在自发性里、在广阔的现在的同时性存在里，也可以有秩序，而且的确也有了秩序。", "en": "There can be order without a succession of moments. There can be order, believe it or not, without your cause and effect. There can be order, and there is order, in spontaneity, and in the simultaneous existence of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0002", "zh": "你们当然知道，连续时间理念在你们的层面上行得通，或者说到目前为止行得通。但当人类变得更有野心时，这种观念对人类就不再行得通了，而在理论上就会被实际舍弃掉，虽然在实际世俗上仍然会以有限的方式被利用，就如同你们实际仍然会发现桌子是有用的一样；虽然理论上你们了解到它不是一个实体，但你们仍然会制造它；此外，即使你们科学家发现一个片刻点接着一个片刻的理论陈旧又过时很久之后，你们仍然会继续使用钟表。", "en": "You understand of course that the theory of successive moments works on your plane, or has worked so far. But as mankind grows even more ambitious then the idea will cease to work for him, and it will be actually discarded on theoretical terms while it is still utilized in its limited fashion in practical mundane terms, as you still find the table useful in practical terms; although theoretically you realize that it is not a solid you still manufacture tables, and you will still use watches long after your scientists discover that the theory of successive passage of moments is antiquated and itself passe.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0039", "zh": "你一定记得我给你的那份有关片刻点和行动本质的资料。你知道那一份资料在这里全部都适用。再一次，你只是感知任何既定行动的一小部分，当你不再感知它的时候，对你来说行动本身似乎就停止了，所以人为的界限于焉树立。", "en": "You must remember the material I gave you concerning moment points, and the nature of action. All of that material you see applies here. Again, you merely perceive a small portion of any given action, and when you cease to perceive it then it seems to you that the action itself ceases, and so an artificial boundary is erected.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第248节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "248", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0058", "zh": "目的是意识本身的扩展，这就自动引导人们认识到，每个意识都是相互联系，对任何人的伤害就是对所有人的伤害。时间根本不是以一系列片刻点的方式存在，这是三维度的幻觉，因此，实际上并没有某一世是活在另一世之前或之后的问题。", "en": "The purpose is the expansion of consciousness itself, and this automatically leads to the knowledge that every consciousness is connected to every other, and that any harm to one is harm to all. Time simply does not exist as a series of moments. This is three-dimensional illusion. Therefore in actuality no one life is lived before nor after another.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第357节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "357", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0072", "zh": "现在。如果与你们自己如此密切相连的人格尚且是这种情形，那么你们或许就能明白，你们的时间观念对于那些从未在你们物质系统中存在过的人格来说，是多么陌生。他们习惯于不以任何时间顺序来体验事件。相反，片刻点被全然体验，种种开展同时打开，而“事件”则被认作是心灵与心理的发生，不一定与任何外在环境相连。", "en": "Now. If such is the case with personalities so closely allied with your own, then you can perhaps understand how alien your idea of time is to personalities that have never existed within your physical system. They are used to experiencing events not in any time sequence. Instead moment points are experienced fully, developments opening simultaneously, and “events” are recognized as psychic and psychological happenings not necessarily connected with any exterior circumstance.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第430节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "430", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0057", "zh": "个体在经历一个片刻点某部分的方式，看起来可能似乎（划线）没有尽头。", "en": "Now. It is possible for an individual to experience a portion of one moment point in such a way that it seems(underlined) there is no end to it.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "存有的细胞：许多片刻点如何聚成一个更大的自己", "note": "第 429 节给了这一页最大的比喻：把一个巨大化的、类人的存有形象投射在午夜的星空上，它看似边界之内的无数行星与恒星就代表片刻点。它们一方面是这个存有的一部分，正如你的细胞是你身体的一部分；另一方面存有的意识能在其中穿行——它们是他自己心理构成之内通往种种经验的门户。而穿行的那一下显然会改变片刻点的性质：那仍是行动在自身之内运作，你理解的时间因素几乎不存在。第 429 节另给一个读法：片刻点也可以代表属于这个存有的种种人格，是它自身意识被派去探索与发现的那些部分，仿佛一个细胞的核能在自己之内旅行；于是存有的边界是想像的，它觉得自己能负荷多少，就纳入多少片刻点——这句要和第 150 节的定义对照着读，「不用过度费力就可以纳入的实相范围」原来就是同一条判据。第 152 节说鲁柏所属的那个全我伸缩极度自如，因此能同时包围更多的片刻点，并用其中特定的一个作为参考点或入口点。第 151 节补上递归那一层：全我不但感知这些无限的片刻点，还从自己投射出片段体与人格到所有这些点上，创造其他自我、其他强烈的焦点，它们各自发展自己的命运与经验，进而以慢动作感知任何一个片刻点；这些被往外投射的人格又会创造新人格，周而复始。", "src": "第 151、152、429 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 152 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 429 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0069", "zh": "现在。如同我告诉过你们的，有某种持续性。无论如何，在广阔的现在之内，总有与你们关于持续性的观念相应的东西；然而那其实是强度的问题。存有本身就由这样的强度组成。只是为了类比起见，想象一个巨大化的存有形象——一个类人的形象——铺展在你们物质宇宙里的任何地方。而如果这形象被投射到午夜的星空上，那么在它看似的边界之内，你们便会看到无数的行星与恒星。让这些代表片刻点。一方面，它们是存有的一部分，就如你们的细胞是你们身体的一部分。另一方面，存有的意识能够穿行于其中。它们是他自己心理构成之内的门户，通往种种经验。", "en": "Now. As I have told you, there is duration of a kind. What would correspond, in any case, to your idea of duration within the spacious present ; it is a matter of intensities however. Now the entity is in itself composed of such intensities. Simply for the sake of analogy, imagine the image, a humanoid one, of an entity giant-sized, spread out anywhere in your physical universe. And if the image were projected against a midnight sky, within its apparent boundaries then you would see a multitude of planets and stars. Let these represent moment points. On one hand they are a part of the entity, as your cells are a portion of your body. On the other hand the entity’s consciousness can travel through these. They are doorways within his own psychological makeup, into experiences.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第429节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "429", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0070", "zh": "这就好像你们能有意识地与自己的每一个细胞达成谅解，并用你们的话说，觉察到它们的未来与它们的过去。这种穿越显然会改变片刻点的性质。这再次是行动在自身之内运作。你们所理解的时间因素几乎不存在。", "en": "It is as if you could consciously come to terms with each of your own cells and become aware, in your terms, of their future and their past. This traveling- through obviously changes the nature of the moment points. It is, again, action working within itself. The time element, as you understand it, hardly exists.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第429节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "429", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0071", "zh": "片刻点也可以代表属于存有的种种人格——它自身意识的一些部分，被它派去进行探索与发现的旅程。这就仿佛一个细胞的核能在其自身之内旅行。存有的边界会出自想象，它觉得自己能应付多少，便纳入多少片刻点。（停顿。）", "en": "Now the moment points could also represent various personalities belonging to the entity, portions of its own consciousness that it sends upon the journeys of exploration and discovery. It is as if the nuclei of a cell could travel through itself. The boundaries of the entity would be imaginary, taking in as many moment points as the entity felt it could handle. (Pause.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第429节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "429", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0021", "zh": "鲁柏所属的那个全我，伸缩极度自如。这个全我的各个部分，已胜过大多数全我的弹性，向外也向内伸展。因此这个全我利用特定的一个片刻点作为参考点或入口点，同时包围更多的片刻点。", "en": "The whole self of which Ruburt is a part is an extremely elastic one. The various portions of this whole self reach outward and inward with much more resilience than most. Therefore this whole self surrounds many more moment points simultaneously, using one moment point in particular as a reference or entry point.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第152节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "152", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0013", "zh": "全我不但感知这些无限的片刻点，而且身为行动的一部分，每一个全我也都从它自己投射出片段体和人格到所有这些片刻点上，因而创造出其他的自我，其他的强烈聚焦点，它们是独立的，各自发展自己的命运和经验，进而以慢动作感知任何一个片刻点。", "en": "The whole self not only perceives these limitless moment points, but being a part of action, each whole self projects fragments and personalities from itself to all these points, creating therefore other egos, other intense focus points which are independent, which work out their own destinies and experiences, which in turn perceive any given moment point in slow motion.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0014", "zh": "内在自我向内看，可是在向内看的同时，又往外看着自己那些为数众多的各个部分。因为行动之内永远还有行动，也因为我们之前说过的三个两难之局，这些被往外投射进入其他感知场域或片刻点的新人格，接着又会创造出新的人格，就这样周而复始不断循环。", "en": "The inner ego looks inward, yet in looking inward it looks outward toward those vast portions of the self. Because there is always action within action, and because of the three dilemmas of which we have spoken earlier, the new personalities projected outward into other fields of perception, or other moment points, these other personalities in turn create new ones, and the cycle is again repeated.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "你的能量在好几个片刻点上同时生成肉身", "note": "这一块把前面的尺度落到「我到底有几个一生」。《个人实相的本质》第 668 节说得最具体：你存在的能量在七个片刻点上侵入三度空间系统，在每一个点上都经验到一看来仿佛孤立的一生；就在这些交会点之外，还有对凌驾其上的整体或多或少全面而统一的认识，那代表多次元的存在。你在 17 世纪有一个存在，对你而言那一生已经过去、已经结束，你以为目前这个存在是它的结果——其实两者同时存在，17 世纪并没有死去。第 672 节把同一件事改写成第二人称：你的存在、那个作为「你自己」的更大意识，与时空交会，同时在许多片刻点里生成肉身；你会把每一次浸入三维存在都叫做一个生命、一个「自己」，而你是其中之一。第 669 节说明其他部分的你此刻在哪：他们的经历潜藏在片刻点的窗户里，而片刻点只是你与所知实相目前的交会点。第 300 节处理转世之间的距离：那趟旅程本身发生在一瞬间，就像从这里投射到波多黎各，你只不过是在转世的情况中更深入那个片刻点，按你们的说法才叫「在那里停留更久」。第 423、424 节给的是选择的语气：赛斯自己没选过时间这种受限的经验，他存有中没有物质经验的部分并不在那个时间系统内运作——那不是他们达不到，只是没有选择那种特定的经验、没有深入过那个片刻点。最后一条是罗的编注：与片刻点资料一起传来的还有「有些系统里，从你们的观点看一瞬可以持久到一个宇宙的一生」，同一个点，长度竟能差到这个地步。", "src": "第 300、423、424、668、669、672、744 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 300 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 423 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 424 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 668 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 669 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 672 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0075", "zh": "再次地，真正发生的是：你存在的能量在七个“片刻点”②（moment points）侵入三度空间系统内。而在每一个点之中，你就会经验到看起来仿佛是孤立的一生。然而，就在这些交会点之外，还有对于“凌驾”其上的整体或多或少的全面而统一的认识，这个整体就代表了那个多次元的存在，而这存在是与各个分别的生命痕迹分开，却又是它的一部分。譬如说，你在17世纪有一个“存在”。对你而言，会显得那个人生已经过去而结束了。你也许相信，目前的“存在”连带它所有能力与挑战，是那过去一生的结果，但事实上两者是同时存在的。17世纪并未死去。你追随着一个单线的历史模式，而且也追随某一种行动为实相，如此完全地与这些认同，以致它们成为你感知的一切。然而，其他的可能行动永远在发生中，并且也与你恰好选择而因之体验的那个一样有效。", "en": "Again, what actually happens is that the energy of your being impinges, say, at seven [moment] points* into the three-dimensional system. At each of these points, what seems to be an isolated life is experienced. Just beyond those intersections, however, there is a more or less unitary and overall recognition of wholeness that “rides” above them. This represents the multidimensional entity that is both apart from and yet part of the separate life-traces. You may have an existence in the seventeenth century, for example. To you it would appear that the life was a past one, finished. You may believe that your current existence, with all of its abilities and challenges, is the result of that past life, yet both exist at once. The seventeenth century is not dead. You follow a one-line pattern of history, pursuing certain actions as reality and identifying with these so completely that they are all you perceive. Other probable actions are always occurring, however, and are quite as valid as the ones which you happen to choose and thus experience.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第668节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "668", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0079", "zh": "如果有意识的信念引起你很大的痛苦，从这个来源可以收到相对的有益信念。你的存在——即为“你自己”的那个更大的意识——与时空交会，它在许多的“片刻点”里将同时生成肉身（见第十九章第六六八节）。你将称这些进入三度空间存在的“侵入”为一个生命，而有其“自己”，而你是其中之一。", "en": "If your conscious beliefs are causing you great distress, countering beneficial beliefs may be received from this source. Your being, the greater consciousness that is yourself, intersects with space and time; it is born in flesh simultaneously at many [moment] “points.” (See the 668th session in Chapter Nineteen.) You would call each of these immersions into three-dimensional existence a life, with its own self. And you are one of these.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第672节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "672", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0076", "zh": "以其自己的方式，那么，你多次元存在的其他部分，也是涉及在与你自己多少相似的经验里，虽然，外表看起来情况也许完全不同，他们的经历是潜藏在片刻点的窗户里——片刻点只是你与所知实相目前的交会点。", "en": "In their own ways, other portions of your multidimensional being are involved in experiences, then, somewhat similar to your own, though on the outside the situation may be completely different. Their progress lies latent within the window of the moment point — the moment point simply being your current intersection with the reality that you know.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第669节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "669", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0048", "zh": "这趟旅程本身发生在一瞬间，就像从这里到波多黎各的一次投射那样。你只不过是在转世的情况中更深入片刻点而已。按照你们的（划线）说法，你在那里停留更久。", "en": "The journey itself is as instantaneous as a projection from here to, say, Puerto Rico. You are simply delving more deeply into the moment point in the reincarnational instance. In your (underlined) terms you are staying there longer.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第300节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "300", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0067", "zh": "我可以通过与我本体中曾直接经验过时间的其他部分沟通，而获得一种概念性的了悟。那是一种受限的经验，我自己并未选择参与其中。我参与过其他一些存在与片刻点，你们或许会觉得那些受限，但那对我是一种挑战。（微笑。）", "en": "I can obtain a conceptual realization through communicating with other portions of my identity that have experienced it directly. It is a confining experience, in which I myself have not chosen to participate. I have participated in other existences and moment points that you might find confining, but that was challenging to me. (Smile.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第423节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "423", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0068", "zh": "不过，我存有中那些没有物质经验的部分，并不在那个时间系统内运作——任何时候都不（微笑），请原谅这个双关语。那并不是他们达不到的。他们只是没有选择那种特定的经验，也没有深入过那个片刻点。", "en": "Those portions of my entity that have not had physical experience, however, do not operate within that time system, at any time (smile), if you will excuse the pun. It is not beyond them. They simply have not chosen the particular experience, nor delved into that moment point.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第424节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "424", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "通道与伪装：从一个系统到另一个系统的参考点", "note": "第 151 节给了一个「为简单起见」的替代定义：片刻点也可以想成从一个系统到另一个系统的参考点，并且当场把它和伪装连上；同节另一段解释这层伪装的意思——同一个片刻点会随感知者不同而不同，定义不跟别的议题相关就没有太大意义。第 152 节说这些点起着通道或入口的作用，通常从某一个活动场域通往另一个。第 219 节讲出谁在走这些通道：出现在你物质宇宙里的这个片刻点，只是广阔现在较大部分的一个小小实现；在梦的状态，当自我从「时间是一系列片刻」的概念里解脱出来，自己的其他部分就能旅行过这些片刻点，那是一趟与你概念中的时间、空间都无关的穿越深度之旅——你透过强度旅行，而这些片刻点像螺旋，穿过去便与自我看来已经发生和尚未发生的过去、未来的行动接触。第 258 节把这套读法用在天文上：那张图里每一颗恒星都代表另一个系统的一个片刻点，它在你系统之内看起来是物质、也只被感知到其实相的最低点，在另一个系统之内却是完全不同的东西；天体作为片刻点符合某些你们数学描述不了的原理，而你会形成自己运作于其中的那个系统——若能如实感知它们，它们就在你的系统之内如实存在。第 419 节由赛斯用自己的存在收尾：他的能量高度集中，以一个强化的团块与片刻点纠缠在一起，也许像一个无限的细胞，同时存在于无穷无尽的维度当中，甚至透过彼此之间的相互连结，从自己的实相穿越其他实相伸到你们的房间里。", "src": "第 151、152、219、258、419 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 152 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 219 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 258 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 419 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "天体即另一个系统的片刻点", "note": "只在把这套说法对到星空、恒星与维度时看", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0040", "zh": "例如，在图中，每一颗恒星代表另一个系统的一个片刻点。从你们的观点来看，它在你们的系统之内看起来是物质，而且在你们的系统之内也以物质的形式存在。但存在另一个系统之内的它，你看，却是完全不同的东西。你们只有感知它实相的最低点，所以我现在告诉你，你们在你们在宇宙中观察到的各种恒星、行星和天体确实存在，但只存在你们的系统之内。", "en": "In the diagram for example, each star would represent a moment point in another system. It appears as matter within your system, from your viewpoint, and exists as matter within your system. But it exists as something entirely different, you see, within another system. You perceive but the lowest point of its reality, so I will tell you now that the various stars and planets and heavenly bodies that you observe in your universe do indeed exist as such, but only within your system.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第258节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "258", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0041", "zh": "你们所谓的维度代表实相被感知的状态。你们感知三维里的实相，你也一瞥在第四维度里的实相。然而，所有的方向都有很多方面。这些天体代表其他系统中的片刻点。不过，当它们被投射到你们的系统时，你们只有在物质方面感知到它们。", "en": "What you call dimensions represent states in which reality is perceived. You perceive reality in three dimensions, and you have a glimpse of reality in a fourth dimension. There are many dimensions however in all directions. These heavenly bodies represent moment points in other systems. As they are projected into your system however, they are only perceived in terms of matter.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第258节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "258", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0043", "zh": "你们必须用你们自己的说法诠释它们。你们形成你们在其内运作的系统。例如，天体对其他系统而言是片刻点。如果你们能够如实感知它们，那么它们实际上就如实存在你们的系统之内。", "en": "You must interpret them in your own terms. You form the system within which you operate. The heavenly bodies for example are moment points to other systems. They actually exist as such within your system if you could perceive them as such.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第258节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "258", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0017", "zh": "为了简单起见，片刻点或许也可以想成从一个系统到另一个系统的参与点。现在你有没有看到，像以前的课解释过的，这里和伪装有关联？", "en": "These moment points may, for simplicity’s sake, also be thought of as reference points from one system to another. Do you see now a connection here with camouflage, as explained in early sessions?", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0018", "zh": "片刻点会被视为伪装，这句话的意思只是说，不同的感知者，就会有不同的感知方式。定义没有太大意义，除非它们跟其他议题相关。为了这个理由，只要时间允许，我就会用你们熟悉的用语，好让你们清楚看见它们的关系。", "en": "The moment point will be seen as camouflage, which simply means that it will be perceived differently according to the perceptors. Definitions have little meaning unless they are related to other issues. For that reason I will try whenever possible to relate terms with which you are familiar in ways so that their relationships will be clearly seen.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0031", "zh": "我们再次开始谈我们的片刻点。现在，这个出现在你们物质宇宙的片刻点，是这个广阔的现在较大部分的一个小小实现。在梦的状态，当自我从时间是一系列的片刻这种概念里解脱出来，那自己的其他部分可以旅行过这些片刻点，然后在这里，你会开始一趟和你的概念中的时间空间无关的、穿越深度的旅行。", "en": "We start once more with our moment point. For now this moment point which appears within your physical universe is but a small materialization of larger portions of the spacious present. In the dreaming state, when the ego is released from its idea of time as a series of moments, then other portions of the self can travel through these moment points, and you have here a journey through depths that have nothing to do with your （underline your） concept of time or space.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0032", "zh": "如我告诉过你的，你透过强度旅行。这些片刻点就像螺旋形的，透过旅行过它们，这些自己的其他部分，根据自我的观点，同时与已经发生和尚未发生的过去和未来的行动接触。", "en": "You journey through intensities, as I have told you. These moment points are like spirals however, and journeying through them these other portions of the self will come in contact with both future and past actions, that have occurred, or will occur, according to the view point of the ego.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第219节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "219", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0066", "zh": "我们以某种方式透过无穷无尽的宇宙为我们自己播种。物质层面来说，你会发现我是比棕色坚果还小的一团东西，因为我的能量高度集中，以一个强化的团块存在着，并与片刻点纠缠在一起，也许就像一个无限的细胞一样，而同时又存在于无穷无尽的维度当中（停顿），甚至透过彼此之间的相互连结，从我自己的实相穿越其他实相，伸展到你们的房间。", "en": "In one way we have seeded ourselves through endless universes. Physically you would find me a mass smaller than a brown nut, for my energy is so highly concentrated. It exists in intensified mass entangled and intertwined with moment points, perhaps like one infinite cell, existing however in endless dimensions at once (pause), and reaching out through interconnections even from my own reality through others to your room.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第419节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "419", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "怎么用：允许自己被那个片刻点包住", "note": "资料里没有名为「片刻点练习」的成套步骤，但第 400、401 节给了两处可操作的说法，都落在创作上：视觉画面会采用另一种形式，如果你全程忠实跟随，画面与它所采用的形式就成为一个片刻点——别让形式被强加在画面上，形式应当由画面应运而生；而形式是由能量在任一时间的特定条件引发的，你若直觉地意识到那种奇迹般的工整、允许自己受到那个特定片刻点的包围，画就会环绕着你形成，方式有点像「我」透过鲁柏的声音形成。第 462 节给的是这条路背后的原理：知觉者被他所知觉的东西改变，同时也改变被知觉的东西，知觉者与知觉从根本上就是同一回事——赛斯说，这里已经接近价值完成与片刻点的含义。第 151 节留了一个日常旁证：艺术对自我往往显得不受时间影响，因为融进它里面的片刻点，多过自我一般能够感知的数量。", "src": "第 151、400、401、462 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 400 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 401 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 462 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0061", "zh": "视觉画面会采用另一种形式，但是如果你全程忠实跟随，那么视觉画面以及它采用的形式，就会变成一个片刻点。（停顿）让视觉画面以形式来表达自己；再说一遍，不要试图将形式强加于视觉画面上面。形式应该要由视觉画面应运而生。", "en": "The vision will take another form, but if you have faithfully followed through, then the vision and its adopted form become one moment point. (Pause.) Allow the vision to express itself in form; again, do not attempt to impose the form upon the vision. The form should grow out of the vision.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第400节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "400", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0062", "zh": "无论何时，形式都是由能量的特定条件所引发。如果你直觉地意识到那种奇迹般的工整，如果你允许自己受到那个特定片刻点的包围，那么就会透过你形成一幅画作，其方式就有点类似透过鲁柏的声音形成我一样。不过，你的画作当然更加显眼。", "en": "The form is caused by a characteristic condition of the energy at any given time. If you are intuitively aware of that miraculous neatness, if you allow yourself to be enveloped within that particular moment point, then the painting will form itself about you in somewhat the same manner that I am formed about Ruburt's voice. But your painting of course will be more visible.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第401节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "401", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0073", "zh": "现在我告诉你们：知觉者被他所知觉的东西改变了，而他同时也改变那被知觉的东西。知觉者与知觉，从根本上说就是同一回事。在这里，我们已经接近价值完成与片刻点的含义。", "en": "Now I tell you that while the perceiver is changed by what he perceives, he also changes that which is perceived. Perceiver and perception, in a basic manner, are one and the same. Here we come close to the meaning of value fulfillment and moment points.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第462节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "462", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0015", "zh": "对自我而言，艺术往往不受时间影响，因为融合在它之内的片刻点，多过于自我一般能够感知的数量。", "en": "Art often appears timeless to the ego because it often merges within it a greater number of moment points than the ego can ordinarily perceive.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "创造与再生：新的意识不断形成新的片刻点", "note": "片刻点不是分完就见底的库存。第 343 节：自己会继续存在，连组成肉体的原料也继续行动；**行动把本身分化成各种自己，然后探索经验的各个片刻点**，因为每一个新的自己实际上都是一个新的行动、一种原始的行动。同一节把镜头拉到最大：你们整个物质宇宙代表了整个总体设计当中的一个片刻点，而这个设计本身不断变化，并没有你们所谓的开始或结束。第 406 节说的是同一件事的反方向：实相及其特征都将视为联合心灵意识的一部分，所有其他意识都源出于此，而这些新出现的意识形成新的片刻点、创造新的价值充盈经验，使整体实相在不断被创造的同时也在创造。第 410 节给的是坐标图：这些坐标形成所有实相，它们是生命力得以透过之自我表达的独一无二的点，伪装沿着坐标冒出来，而片刻点为进一步的表达和发展提供无限的机会——实相的内在构造远比你们所知的外在伪装复杂。", "src": "第 343、406、410 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 343 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 406 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 410 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-057-e0053", "zh": "这个自己在继续存在，即使是组成肉体的原料也继续行动。行动把本身分化成各种自我（selves），接着探索经验的各个片刻点，因为每个新的自己实际上都是一个新的行动，一种原始的行动。", "en": "The self goes on. Even the stuff of the physical body however continues to act. Action divides itself into various selves, and then explores the moment points of experience, for each new self is indeed a new action, an original act.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0055", "zh": "然而，这个结构与强度毫无关系。好，我说得慢一点：你们整个物质宇宙代表了整个总体设计中的一个片刻点，不过，这个设计本身不断变化，并没有你们所谓的开始或结束。", "en": "The structure has nothing to do with the intensity however. Now, very slowly: your entire physical universe represents one moment point in a whole overall design. Yet the design itself is ever-changing, and there is no beginning or end to it in your terms.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第343节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "343", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0063", "zh": "从更宽广的角度来看，实相一词和我将提供给你们的那些特征，都将视为联合心灵意识的重要部分，所有其他意识都源自于这个心灵意识。这些新出现的意识形成了新的片刻点，也创造新的价值充盈经验，而这些经验又不断创造出整体实相，即使这个整体实相也仍在持续创造。", "en": "In larger terms, the word reality and those characteristics that I will give you as attributed to it, will be seen as part and parcel of a unified psychic consciousness, from which all other consciousness emerges. These emerging consciousness form new moment points, create new value fulfillment experiences that constantly allow the overall reality to be created even as it creates.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第406节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "406", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-057-e0065", "zh": "这些坐标形成所有实相。它们是独一无二的点，生命力可以透过它们自我表达。伪装沿着坐标出现（停顿），片刻点为进一步的表达和发展提供无限的机会。实相的内在构造远比你们所知的外在伪装要复杂得多。", "en": "These coordinates form all realities. They are unique points through which vitality expresses itself. Camouflages spring up (pause) along the coordinates, and moment points offer endless opportunities for further expression and development. The inner fabric of reality is far more complicated than outer camouflage as you know it.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第410节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "410", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [], "books": [{"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 19}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 12}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 2}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 2}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 1}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1974], "stats": {"blocks": 10, "quotes": 59, "reading": 0, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 1}};
